  "name": "Recursive Research",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Recursive research up to PhD level across any domain (science, tech, business, arts, humanities). Source tiering (Tier 1/2/3/rejected), WDM + Munger inversion for autonomous decisions, and disk checkpointing to survive context compaction. Works with web sources, local files, or mixed mode — interactive setup asks for seed, priority/excluded sources, and cycle cap before starting.",
  "longDescription": "Installs with `claude plugin install recursive-research@claude-community` from `Anjos2/recursive-research`.\n\nVersion: 2.2.0 · License: MIT · Author: Joseph Huayhualla (@Anjos2)\n\nRecursive research up to PhD level across any domain (science, tech, business, arts, humanities). Source tiering (Tier 1/2/3/rejected), WDM + Munger inversion for autonomous decisions, and disk checkpointing to survive context compaction. Works with web sources, local files, or mixed mode — interactive setup asks for seed, priority/excluded sources, and cycle cap before starting.",
